<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 137 0 R/Alt(Same constant world-energy benchmark and logarithmic years axis as page 25. Alternative lead- and beryllium-based 2011 conceptual 1 GW net-electric plants, at 90 percent capacity factor. Subtract initial fleet loading before depletion by nuclear transmutation. With ideal recovery, 95 Mt Pb reserves leave about 45 years; identified Pb resources above 2 Gt give more than 30353 years. Beryllium resources are reported only as above 100 kt; their total is unknown, so no lifetime is assigned. The illustrative fleet needs 2.7 Mt initially. USGS reports more than 100 kt Be resources, not a total resource ceiling or world reserve estimate.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[9]/Pg 208 0 R>>
